    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a primary focus on exploiting high-ceiling matchups against weaker arms. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the charge with an elite 81.88 efficiency score; he benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against Alcantara, while his spot at the top of the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. Further down the lineup, **Josh Lowe** (71.68) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.34) represent opportunistic plays; both are bolstered by favorable wind conditions and, crucially, matchups against pitchers with slow deliveries that enhance their stolen base upside\u2014a priority given our roster's emphasis on speed. **Miguel Vargas** and **Nolan Schanuel** also project well today, each drawing significant value from the soft 5.31\u20135.50 xERA profiles of their respective opponents, allowing them to capitalize on high-leverage lineup slots.\n\nWhile the bottom of the order carries some risk, our bench management remains disciplined. **Marcell Ozuna** was the hardest player to keep out of the starting nine; his 59.97 score was respectable, but his sub-optimal lineup placement and the superior situational metrics of our UTIL option, **Josh Jung** (64.67), pushed him to the bench. We must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Drake Baldwin**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Josh Lowe**, and **Heliot Ramos**; should any of these players move down in their respective batting orders, their scores will regress, necessitating a quick pivot. Additionally, despite their talent, we are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker** today as they face formidable arms in Webb and Lambert, respectively, which suppresses their immediate upside compared to the rest of the stack.",
